intro='# Phase 11A.5 — final selection and conditional integration\n\nUpdated 2026-11-17. This report supersedes the initial Stage A hold; historical reports remain under evidence/stage-a-reports/. User authorization permits source-verified approved directions and a documented PH07 choice, while expressly holding PH01 until final hero approval. No purchases, permission requests, deployment or Phase 11B work occurred.\n\n'
rows='| Placement | Current state |\n|---|---|\n'+''.join(f"| {i['id']} · {i['placement']} | {status[i['id']]} |\n" for i in all)
selection=intro+'## Placement decisions\n\n'+rows+'''\nSix photos are integrated: PH02, PH05, PH07-B, PH08, PH10, PH11. Five placements remain schematic: PH01, PH03, PH04, PH06, PH09. The seven approved directions were assessed individually; approval of direction did not override two source-specific rights holds.\n\n## Hero — two replacement candidates for final visual approval\n\nOpen [FINAL_SELECTION_BOARD.html](FINAL_SELECTION_BOARD.html), [desktop studies](screenshots/final-selection-1440.png) or [mobile studies](screenshots/final-selection-390.png). Neither candidate is installed in public/ or referenced by heroMedia. Live typography, buttons, heights, overlays and animations remain untouched.\n\n**R1 — Metehan Özaras, sunrise excavator silhouette.** [Publisher](https://www.pexels.com/photo/silhouette-of-excavator-at-sunrise-11562423/), [licence](https://www.pexels.com/license/), [detailed terms](https://www.pexels.com/terms-of-service/). Native 3648 × 2736, downloaded and fully decoded. Proposed desktop source crop: x=0, y=650, width=2600, height=1463; mobile study covers that derivative at 70% 50%. Quiet left sky with machine/sun toward the right, no prominent branding observed. This is the quieter, scenic option: the distant excavator is small, and human silhouettes are not identifiable. It trades equipment detail for atmosphere. No reflection or invented scene.\n\n**R2 — saravut vanset, large mining shovel at dusk.** [Publisher](https://www.pexels.com/photo/yellow-and-black-heavy-equipment-at-the-site-during-sunset-10410019/), [licence](https://www.pexels.com/license/), [detailed terms](https://www.pexels.com/terms-of-service/). Native 5520 × 3680, downloaded and fully decoded. Stronger machinery scale and cinematic dusk light; no prominent manufacturer wordmark observed. The original is LEFT weighted. The study explicitly proposes horizontal reflection, allowed as a copyright modification, to place machine mass RIGHT and sky LEFT. This change needs visual approval; it is unsuitable if mirrored engineering details are unacceptable. Mobile retains machine mass/tracks and sacrifices extended bucket/boom detail. No hidden retouching or AI generation. Small distant people are not identifiable.\n\nNeither source perfectly solves every criterion without a tradeoff: R1 has a small subject; R2 requires explicit approval of reflection. Recommend choosing between the calm scenic R1 and equipment-led R2 rather than pretending that a branded result meets the brief. The study overlay supports comparison; final in-page acceptance remains pending.\n\nGoogle Images was attempted at its image-search endpoint, which this environment could not access. Original-publisher web/image research was used instead. Do not claim successful Google Images access. Rejected additional results include Matt Seymour's prominent Hitachi boom, Vadym Alyekseyenko's Komatsu shot, Abhisek Tripathy's Liugong machine, Charles Criscuolo's Deere machine, D Goug's CAT machine and Giulia Botan's branded portrait. Search/preview labels alone were insufficient.\n\n## PH07 — cleaner alternative selected\n\nPH07-B by Edge2Edge Media ([publisher](https://unsplash.com/photos/silver-and-black-metal-tools-qHhJkxare7A)) replaces the initially proposed shraga kopstein fittings image. Native 4093 × 2724. The neutral silver/white palette and central fastener are clearer than PH07's crowded warm/green specular reflections. Both depict industrial hardware, but the cleaner alternative better supports surrounding navy/amber typography without competing colour highlights. Black-and-white appearance is in the source, not a new site palette. Generic nuts/bolts are labelled illustrative stock, never actual Zieve stock or promised product availability. Both are shown in the comparison board. Final review of the integrated crop is still welcome.\n\n## PH02 versus PH10\n\nThe introduction uses a suspended round multi-bore component in a 5:6 editorial frame, with the worker profile physically excluded from the public image derivative. Manufacturing uses a long horizontal machined shaft and closer rear-view worker in 4:3. Different objects, distance, framing and gestures make them sufficiently distinct; the same photographer provides tonal continuity. They do not represent Zieve employees or manufacturing capability.\n'''
(root/'IMAGE_SELECTION_REPORT.md').write_text(selection)
