assess={
'PH02':'Publisher file 2965258, Kateryna Babaieva, Free licence link and original download verified. The original includes a worker partial profile; the physically cropped public 5:6 derivative (x=700, y=54, 2800×3360 native crop) excludes that person. No portrait permission is inferred. No identifiable logo or staff claim in the displayed crop. Intended use is anonymous technical context integrated into an editorial section. No separate release certificate was exposed by the publisher; do not claim one exists or reuse as an employee testimonial.',
'PH05':'Publisher file 9KeG7W4cI5U, Hazel J, explicitly linked to the standard Unsplash licence and free download, not Unsplash+. No identifiable person, readable brand or distinctive artwork observed. Generic process infrastructure used as application context; no production, ownership or supply-brand claim.',
'PH07-B':'Publisher file qHhJkxare7A, Edge2Edge Media, explicitly standard Unsplash licence/free download. Full native JPEG inspected: generic neutral nuts/bolts, no people or brand. Used inside the designed solutions section with copy, not distributed as a standalone stock product. No inventory availability claim.',
'PH08':'Publisher file 33122148, Volker Braun, Free Pexels link/original download verified. Distant aerial handling/extraction scene, no recognizable people, brand marks or artwork observed. Generic industry context only; not a verified gold mine, Zimbabwe location, Zieve operation or client.',
'PH10':'Publisher file 2760241, Kateryna Babaieva, Free Pexels link/original download verified. Rear-view worker with no visible face/name. Machinery badge at far background is not readable as a brand in the displayed crop. Generic engineering context only. No independent per-file model/property release certificate supplied; no employee endorsement or company-facility claim.',
'PH11':'Publisher file 36514665, Psilo Cybe, Free Pexels link/original download verified. Grain-handling structures without identifiable people, readable brands or artwork observed. Generic storage/handling context, not a named facility or Zieve/customer installation.'}
rights=intro+'''## Verification standard and limitations\n\nThis is a source/file/intended-use record, not legal advice, a model/property-release certificate or blanket permission for future uses. Each production file was traced from its individual original publisher page to its linked licence and download, decoded at native resolution, visually inspected, hashed and assessed against the actual planned generic website use. Direction approval is recorded separately from licence conditions and final visual acceptance. No watermark/paid preview, Google result, AI image or publisher PDF image is shipped.\n\n[Pexels detailed terms](https://www.pexels.com/terms-of-service/) §5 grants downloading, use, copying and adaptation for commercial/noncommercial work subject to its prohibited uses. §6 makes attribution optional. Crucially, §5 restricts commercial use of content depicting brands in relation to goods/services and disclaims independently obtained additional consents. That stricter text was reviewed alongside the [short licence page](https://www.pexels.com/license/); the summary alone was not treated as clearance. This is why PH03 and PH09 are held despite creative direction approval. No assumption that old photographs are CC0 was made from their publication date.\n\n[Unsplash licence](https://unsplash.com/license) allows free commercial downloading and modification, with optional attribution, excluding competing image services/unchanged resale. [Unsplash terms](https://unsplash.com/terms) §5 excludes separate rights in recognizable people, trademarks and artwork. The specific PH05 and PH07-B pages explicitly link the standard licence, not a sponsored paid/Unsplash+ item; downloads match the listed subjects/native files. Both intended uses avoid identifiable people/brands/artwork and add accurate context.\n\nAll integrated photos retain visible contributor/publisher credits in their existing figure captions, although those platform licences do not require attribution. Captions expressly say “Illustrative stock photo”; alt text describes the object and disclaims Zieve ownership/staff/inventory as applicable. This does not turn the source into Zieve-owned imagery or authorize an endorsement. No permissions were requested on the user's behalf.\n\n'''
verification=[]
